+Concise Bounded Description
+---------------------------
+
+To extract the information a graph holds about a single resource, use
+:meth:`~rdflib.graph.Graph.cbd`. It returns the *Concise Bounded
+Description* (CBD) of the resource, as defined in the `W3C member submission
+<https://www.w3.org/Submission/CBD/>`_. The CBD is a new ``Graph`` made of:
+
+* every triple whose subject is the resource, and
+* for each blank node object of those triples, recursively, every triple whose
+  subject is that blank node.
+
+Following blank nodes means that the description includes the complete
+structure hanging off the resource, while URI references are not followed.
+
+::
+
+    >>> from rdflib import Graph, BNode, Literal, Namespace
+    >>> EX = Namespace("http://example.org/")
+    >>> g = Graph()
+    >>> g.add((EX.alice, EX.knows, EX.bob))
+    >>> g.add((EX.alice, EX.address, BNode("addr")))
+    >>> g.add((BNode("addr"), EX.city, Literal("Paris")))
+    >>> g.add((EX.bob, EX.name, Literal("Bob")))
+    >>> cbd = g.cbd(EX.alice)
+    >>> len(cbd)
+    3
+
+The source graph is not modified. Passing a plain string is accepted and is
+converted to a :class:`~rdflib.term.URIRef`.
+
